Over the 1 h 13 min the planner did not see:
The planner gave no TTFT figure for any step: no prefill speed was learned to price a TTFT from: none under a queue, or, where the prefill pods never queued, only the rate a pod computed, which prices the knee as a lower bound and no TTFT, or one read only at prompts other than the step's (VPPromptNotCovered); fit on more (a larger split, or a longer recording) (refused: NoPrefillCapacity in 15).
mean TPOT: within 20% of measured in 15 of the 15 five-minute steps scored (a figure, and enough measured requests); no overall lean (median ratio 0.98). p90 TPOT not scored in 10: the measured p90 fell in a histogram bucket wider than 20% of its lower edge, too wide to place it, with the prediction inside it or within 20% of its edge; in the measured histogram bucket itself in 10, 10 ms to 20 ms (2.0x wide): consistent at the bucket's resolution, not within 20%. To measure it, give the histogram finer edges: the router's metrics.requestTPOTBuckets in the EndpointPickerConfig (an llm-d-router build after v1.0.0), or vLLM's --custom-histogram-buckets (v0.32.0 and later). Edges about 15% apart place p90 and p95 within 20%.
None of these figures falls within the conditions our own accuracy benchmarks cover (docs/guides/capacity-planner/accuracy.md): this check is the evidence for this fleet.
